From: JohanR7 <143104864+JohanR7@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 20:21:49 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] CH03: sensor alerts with log and e-mail listeners

Add mycodo/utils/sensor_alerts.py (SensorAlert, AlertListener,
SensorAlertNotifier with attach/detach and once-per-episode delivery,
LogAlertListener, EmailAlertListener). The bang-bang Function raises a
missing_measurement alert when no usable reading is available (now also
for None/[] results, which used to raise) and a critically_dry alert
below the new alert_critical_moisture option; alert_email adds an
e-mail listener that reuses DaemonControl.send_email. A failing listener
is logged and does not stop the others. Tests for AC1-AC9.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
